{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
  "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in case 07-1601, Burlington Northern and Santa Fe Railway Company et al. v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, suppose that it's Shell's truck -- that isn't this case, but suppose it's Shell's truck, and every time they make a delivery the driver catches the waste in a can, four or five gallons, and dumps it in the creek. Is Shell liable there under the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell Oil Company",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SULLIVAN: Justice Kennedy, Shell might well be liable there, but not under 107(a)(3), rather under 107(a)(2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: What if Shell went out of business and it had some stuff left in the tanks? At that point, they might very well hire somebody to do exactly what you're saying."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. Sullivan, would it be altogether different if, instead of the FOB destination term, Shell continued as owner of the product until it had gone from the hose or whatever delivers it, so that there is no transfer of ownership until the delivery is complete?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell Oil Company",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SULLIVAN: Yes, Justice Ginsburg, that would be a different case. That would be a case like the so-called formulator cases, of which United States against Aceto from the 8th Circuit is paradigmatic. And in that case the key is that the company arranging -- the company was held liable for arranging to dispose of waste where it owned the product throughout a manufacturing process, sent it out to a formulator, but got it back as its own product, knowing that inherent in the formulation process was the creation of waste material. So Shell would have been the owner of the waste."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if Shell had a choice between two companies to do the delivery. One would deliver it with no spillage whatsoever, but the other would deliver it with a certain amount, a small amount of spillage. And Shell chose the latter because it was cheaper. Would it not be arranging under those circumstances?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell Oil Company",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SULLIVAN: It might well be because there would be an economic benefit to Shell from the arrangement for shipment in the leaky truck. That would be quite a different case from this one. There was no economic benefit to Shell from the leaks here. In fact, Shell did everything possible, so far as the record shows, to prevent spills."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Ms. Sullivan, can I interrupt you? Because I'm still puzzled by your answer to Justice Alito. Are you conceding that if in this case Shell had an alternative carrier who would not have spilled a bit, that then there would be liability?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell Oil Company",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SULLIVAN: No, we are not, Justice Stevens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Burlington Northern and Santa Fe Railway Company et al.",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0000-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAHONEY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I would like to start with section 912 of the Restatement because I think it really helps to demonstrate that the trial court fully understood and properly applied the common law standards that govern the determination of apportionment in a pollution case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you point to me the part of the district court opinion that conflicts with the part that I remember so well?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the trial court very specifically rejected the government's claims of waiver saying, yes, apportionment was at issue here throughout the case"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I suppose the district court, if it wanted additional evidence, could have said, I want additional evidence on this point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government could have filed a motion to amend under Rule 52. They in fact filed a motion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I could begin with the issue of arranger liability. The Ninth Circuit distinguished what it referred to as the useful product cases and made it clear that it would not impose arranger liability on Shell simply under the theory that Shell had sold a useful product that was later disposed of in a way that contaminated the environment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you don't -- but maybe you do claim, I'm not sure -- that Shell actually could, in effect get damages from its deliverer as a result of the -- the deliverer's incidental spillage. Is that your position?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well you have discharged, but you -- the question is whether it's disposal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: If you had a situation, for instance, where the trash company was hauling waste and intended to dispose of it in a more classic sense by dumping it at a landfill, but along the way the truck leaked, and some of the items spilled out -- JUSTICE SOUTER: When? MR. STEWART: -- I think everybody acknowledges that there is disposal there, and I think we would also say that a company that contracted with that trash hauler, knowing that the vehicle tended to leak trash on -- on every delivery, could be said to have arranged for not only the ultimate disposal, but --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: I think it is a combination of knowledge and control. Knowledge might be sufficient, but knowledge and control together form a basis for arranger liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you a question about your argument that the Petitioners waived their apportionment argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court found and the circuit court also found -- the circuit court's finding is on page 36-A of the Petitioner's appendix -- that there is no dispute that the harm here is divisible; that is, there -- the -- the harm here is capable of apportionment. That is not disputed before this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are meticulous findings, 20 pages of findings, based on record evidence from the government's witnesses and from the extensive expert testimony that both Shell and the railroads put in that went to the apportionment issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Shell",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Shell argued --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I'm not sure I know what it means to say it's a divisible harm."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7b2604044bbc-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I'm really concerned about the time and the white light, but I'm -- I'm not sure you answered the Chief Justice's hypothetical about $2 million, which is an initial clean-up that has to be expended no matter how large the -- the spill was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1601",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "7b2604044bbc52708634b47d7edb4b424781e618474d89ca3b4a8a5beb2c11e3",
